{
  "description": "A family-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that inspects the trained HSTU recommender through the host ModelView interface. It returns measured metrics with explicit definitions and builds an interpretation prompt grounded in those measurements.",
  "motivation": "Make model diagnosis useful for iterative improvement while preserving benchmark comparability, HSTU compatibility, and the distinction between observable interaction patterns and unavailable user traits.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Use view.model as the actual trained network and preserve item_emb, log2feats(sequence), and predict_score(features, items). Run probes in evaluation mode without gradients, restoring the previous training mode afterward. Mask padding and invalid targets; for sequence readout, use the final nonpadding position in left-padded histories. Possible probes include positive–negative score margins, representation norms, and recommendation coverage, each reported with its definition, sample count, and limitations. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; mark unavailable attributes as unobserved. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category. Keep one independently trained HSTU checkpoint per category, consistent with the embedded predictor. Model selection remains the host's macro validation HR@10 across all four categories.",
  "pseudocode": "DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n  run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n    save model training state; enter eval mode and no_grad\n    for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n      features = view.log2feats(sequence)\n      identify valid nonpadding positions and targets\n      score positives and negatives using view.predict_score\n      accumulate defined diagnostic measurements over valid entries\n    restore model training state\n    return {metrics: aggregated measurements, metric_definitions: definitions and limitations}\n\ndiagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n  include measured metrics and their definitions\n  request evidence-grounded interpretations and HSTU-compatible hypotheses\n  distinguish observations from hypotheses and unavailable information\n  preserve single-model training and fixed benchmark constraints",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines explicit diagnostic definitions with a family-specific compatibility contract and strict observability constraints.",
    "negative": "Primarily an integration and measurement protocol rather than a new recommendation algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support more reliable architecture and optimization experiments by linking proposed changes to measurable model behavior.",
    "negative": "Diagnostic improvements do not establish ranking improvements; proposals still require validation under the fixed evaluator."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces are narrow, and most probes can reuse existing model features and scoring methods.",
    "negative": "Correct padding masks, feature shapes, full-catalog scoring, and checkpoint–predictor consistency require careful implementation."
  }
}
